   "text": "I read the structure as a macrocyclic peptide and wrote the SMILES by tracing the ring and then assigning stereo from the wedges.\n\n**Ring (traced from the Asn residue):**\n- Asn, with its side-chain CONH2, has its alpha NH acylated by a succinyl linker, C(=O)CH2CH2C(=O).\n- The succinyl linker connects to the Lys epsilon-NH, which continues through (CH2)4 to the Lys alpha carbon, bearing a C-terminal CONH2.\n- The Lys alpha NH is acylated by the Trp carbonyl, so the Trp NH is acylated by the Pro carbonyl.\n- The Pro ring nitrogen is acylated by the cyclohexylglycine carbonyl.\n- The cyclohexylglycine NH is acylated by the Asn carbonyl, which closes the ring.\n\n**Substituents:**\n- Trp carries a 3-indolylmethyl side chain.\n- Pro carries a 1,2,3-triazol-1-yl group at C4, a 4-substituted triazole bearing a 4-(thiophen-2-yl)phenyl group.\n\n**Stereochemistry:**\n- I assigned each centre from the drawn wedges and hashes: Asn, Lys, Trp and Pro alpha carbons come out as the L-configuration, the Chg alpha carbon from its wedge, and the Pro C4 centre from the wedge to the triazole nitrogen.\n- I checked each @/@@ against the drawing, and the Lys centre needed the @@ form.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)C[C@@H]1NC(=O)CCC(=O)NCCCC[C@@H](C(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccccc23)NC(=O)[C@@H]4C[C@H](n5cc(-c6ccc(cc6)-c7cccs7)nn5)CN4C(=O)[C@H](C8CCCCC8)NC1=O"
